{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/658829-we-broke-time-spoilers-sts-only","id":658829,"title":"We Broke Time (spoilers, sts only)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-09T19:54:03-07:00","id":658829,"title":"We Broke Time (spoilers, sts only)","content":"So... I was doing some research into the old hints and tidbits from the developers, in light of the new revelations within Sothis Ascends. In particular, there were a few really specifically worded things CAS said. One, to paraphrase, was &quot;none of the shan'iatu who created the arisen became judges after area fell&quot;. Well, that could be true, but... in Sothis Ascends, we have actual time travel mechanics. Indeed, jumping back to Sothic turns prior to the current one is clearly something the Shan'iatu should be able to do with Utterances, if even Mummies can. So... we go back to one of the first spoiler things said about the masters of the arisen--that they are demigod sorcerers who, as the dev said, BROKE TIME. So... is it time to fully accept the theory that time travel shenanigans is clearly involved? Is it possible the Shani'atu became the judges BEFORE irem was created? That humans at the end of the Empire were capable of the Rite of Return that made them into gods AND travel back in time/become timeless? If the deceived book mentions Irem erasing stars and rewriting the Heavens, did the Scroll of Ages get rewritten? Was the wording deliberate, so that we'd get caught up in more red herrings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T20:06:47-07:00","id":658847,"title":"","content":"Eh, maybe? I mean, there are plenty of inconsistencies in the Shan'iatu=Judges theory. Only 35 Shan'iatu completed the Rite, Arisen find their powers don't work against those made by the same Shan'iatu (which is explicitly described as not being the same as their respective Judges), the Shan'iatu were sorted by Guild but the Judges are sorted by Decree, and so on.<br /> <br /> I'm personally operating under the assumption that the Shan'iatu never became the Judges, and the Judges in Duat are the Judges of Life described by the Book of the Deceived. Said Book does mention the Judges, well, judging souls in Duat.<br /> <br /> It will be interesting to see what Dreams of Avarice has to say on the matter when it finally releases. Apotheosis is meant to allow you to finally remember Duat, so if anyone has anything definitive to say on the cosmology, it will be the Heretic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/658829-we-broke-time-spoilers-sts-only#post658829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That <b>humans</b> at the end of the Empire were capable of the Rite of Return that made them into gods AND travel back in time/become timeless?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T20:20:32-07:00","id":658854,"title":"","content":"Its very tough to sort through, but there hasn't been too much theory updates since the explicitly existent time travel was revealed. I'm glad that the PCs aren't supposed to know much at this point. Right now, my PCs are slowly remembering experiences with the Deceived, so have three main theories: a) the judges are not real, but merely a religious ideology implanted in them by the shan'iatu that the arisen have followed blindly all this time, and its the shan'iatu that screw them over not the Judges.. B) the Judges are cruel dictator gods, who may or may not be the shan'iatu, but otherwise clearly are masters of the arisen and should be cast aside or overthrown (which could be the shan'iatu's end goal and not a past feat), or C) the Judges are real, the Arisen did dirty deals with Ammut for their immortality and blasphemed the cosmos, and the Judges are protecting the world from the Rite and its creations, as well as punishing the arisen so complicit in enacting the rite. Thankfully, only one has any inkling that time travel is real, so that factor hasn't been added. Still, I figure it'll need to be addressed at some point, how time travel and/or breaking time is part of the story, since it has been mentioned by a developer and is canon at least via utterance (if not always during Sothic turns).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T21:55:30-07:00","id":658920,"title":"","content":"Haha, your players must be way more interested in the cosmology than mine. The meret in my game have been playing weekly sessions for a year now, and the most they've delved into Mummy's background was when they formulated the theory, &quot;What if for every Arisen the Shan'iatu made, they had to create a Shuankhsen to power said Arisen?&quot; I don't think they've even touched on the nature of the Judges, let alone begun formulating theories on the Judges' origins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}